=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D
Casting and seeking crew for "Dance For Your Life," a dystopian short film =
set at a dance academy where a diverse class of dancers must compete to sur=
vive under an authoritarian regime. Choreography carries much of the film=
=E2=80=99s meaning, so dancers are central to the story.


- Joy in 'Dance For Your Life' ()
20s, Black, a trained ballet dancer at the core of defiance against oppress=
ion. Must have significant ballet dance experience and be comfortable perfo=
rming a traditional ballet solo. Ballet experience is required, acting expe=
rience is preferred; role will additionally require significant emotional r=
ange.

https://www.backstage.com/casting/dance-for-your-life-3328068/?role_id=3D56=
63456&utm_source=3Ddigest&utm_medium=3Demail&utm_campaign=3Dsaved-search&ut=
m_content=3Drecommended-jobs


- Ian in 'Dance For Your Life' ()
20s, a jazz dancer and fierce figure of rebellion. Dance experience require=
d; acting experience preferred but not strictly necessary; must be comforta=
ble performing a lengthy jazz solo. Outside of dance capability, must also =
be able to carry a passionate relationship with the female lead at the film=
=E2=80=99s center.

https://www.backstage.com/casting/dance-for-your-life-3328068/?role_id=3D56=
63459&utm_source=3Ddigest&utm_medium=3Demail&utm_campaign=3Dsaved-search&ut=
m_content=3Drecommended-jobs


- Dylan in 'Dance For Your Life' ()
20s, Black, preferably with locs. Some dance experience required. He is a l=
eader of rebellion within the dance academy, undoubtedly a role model to ot=
hers, and he is the first to openly rebel against the oppressive new regime=
. Therefore, he is expected to be able to represent outward rage and intern=
al vulnerability, ultimately exploding into a vicious dance solo that becom=
es a rallying cry for artistic freedom.

https://www.backstage.com/casting/dance-for-your-life-3328068/?role_id=3D56=
63460&utm_source=3Ddigest&utm_medium=3Demail&utm_campaign=3Dsaved-search&ut=
